1
00:00:13,743 --> 00:00:21,925
[SPEAKER_00]: I want to discuss right attention, yoniso, manasikāra.

2
00:00:23,145 --> 00:00:29,247
[SPEAKER_00]: The Buddha praises this quality many, many times.

3
00:00:29,307 --> 00:00:32,348
[SPEAKER_00]: It's essential in the practice.

4
00:00:34,148 --> 00:00:37,209
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, it's one of the prerequisites for the right view as well.

5
00:00:37,649 --> 00:00:38,249
[SPEAKER_01]: One out of two.

6
00:00:40,284 --> 00:00:59,477
[SPEAKER_00]: And he says, because I do not see even a single thing that so-called as unarisen wholesome qualities to arise and arisen unwholesome qualities to decline as right attention for one who attends carefully, unarisen wholesome qualities arise and arisen unwholesome qualities...

7
00:00:59,497 --> 00:01:01,099
[SPEAKER_00]: He just says, one who attends properly.

8
00:01:01,499 --> 00:01:08,804
[SPEAKER_01]: Sorry, one who attends... Not careful, because people will think all they need to do is be careful and they'll see the truth.

9
00:01:09,993 --> 00:01:14,895
[SPEAKER_01]: No, you actually need to know where you're supposed to attend, thus attend it properly.

10
00:01:15,615 --> 00:01:16,175
[SPEAKER_01]: Or rightly.

11
00:01:16,676 --> 00:01:17,636
[SPEAKER_01]: Rightly, exactly.

12
00:01:17,656 --> 00:01:18,776
[SPEAKER_01]: Attend it rightly.

13
00:01:22,798 --> 00:01:25,759
[SPEAKER_00]: There are two, these two conditions for arising of right view.

14
00:01:26,779 --> 00:01:26,999
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

15
00:01:27,039 --> 00:01:30,621
[SPEAKER_00]: The utterance of another and proper attention.

16
00:01:31,681 --> 00:01:33,282
[SPEAKER_00]: These are the two conditions.

17
00:01:33,302 --> 00:01:33,782
[SPEAKER_00]: Rightly.

18
00:01:42,131 --> 00:01:51,475
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, when he, he, he usually speaks after partition, or depends origination, he uses that proper attention, danger to that.

19
00:01:53,295 --> 00:01:54,456
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, I'll just give one example.

20
00:01:55,636 --> 00:02:00,558
[SPEAKER_00]: The last is, this can be found in the connected discourses, Samyutta Nikāla.

21
00:02:07,157 --> 00:02:14,022
[SPEAKER_00]: Because, before my enlightenment, while I was still a bodhisattva, not yet fully enlightened, it occurred to me.

22
00:02:14,883 --> 00:02:20,206
[SPEAKER_00]: Alas, this world has fallen into trouble, in that it is born, ages and dies.

23
00:02:21,087 --> 00:02:22,888
[SPEAKER_00]: It passes away and is reborn.

24
00:02:25,030 --> 00:02:29,533
[SPEAKER_00]: Yet it does not understand the escape from this suffering, headed by aging and death.

25
00:02:30,694 --> 00:02:34,957
[SPEAKER_00]: Where now will an escape be discerned from this suffering, headed by aging and death?

26
00:02:36,685 --> 00:02:41,767
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, because it occurred to me, when what exists does aging and death come to be.

27
00:02:42,647 --> 00:02:45,248
[SPEAKER_00]: But what is aging and death determined?

28
00:02:46,729 --> 00:02:51,691
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, because, through proper attention, there took place in me a breakthrough by wisdom.

29
00:02:52,631 --> 00:02:55,233
[SPEAKER_00]: When there is birth, aging and death come to be.

30
00:02:56,073 --> 00:02:59,974
[SPEAKER_00]: Aging and death has birth as its determination.

31
00:03:01,495 --> 00:03:05,857
[SPEAKER_00]: So, through proper attention, there took place in me a breakthrough by wisdom.

32
00:03:08,494 --> 00:03:09,175
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

33
00:03:09,695 --> 00:03:32,131
[SPEAKER_01]: So, as pretty much every other sutta, well, pretty much every sutta, people can either read it kind of superficially, so to speak, and then read that passage as, oh, okay, so the Buddha properly, you know, he was carefully attending, he was really thinking about it, and then he figured it out.

34
00:03:33,192 --> 00:03:36,575
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, yeah, it can read like that.

35
00:03:37,452 --> 00:03:50,198
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you actually take every sutta to be a phenomenological description of the nature of experience, nature of things, thus, if understood, a person would be at least a sotāpanna, if not more.

36
00:03:51,218 --> 00:03:53,299
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, in that case, you would approach it quite differently.

37
00:03:53,539 --> 00:03:54,940
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if he says...

38
00:03:54,960 --> 00:04:06,525
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if he used yoniso manasikāra there, which he did, if he used the same term, that proper attention or the right attention, means proper attention is that which reveals

39
00:04:09,932 --> 00:04:17,718
[SPEAKER_01]: It reveals the principle of dependent origination.

40
00:04:17,778 --> 00:04:24,883
[SPEAKER_01]: The principle that basically has its two factors that are simultaneously present.

41
00:04:25,984 --> 00:04:36,072
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it says, with what this condition has this... well, with what this condition is aging and death being manifest.

42
00:04:36,801 --> 00:04:42,308
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, you know, you are aging and dying simply by being alive.

43
00:04:44,470 --> 00:04:45,632
[SPEAKER_00]: Simply by being... Yeah.

44
00:04:45,832 --> 00:04:49,256
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what is the simultaneously present condition for that state?

45
00:04:49,857 --> 00:04:52,800
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the fact that you are manifested in this human existence.

46
00:04:53,001 --> 00:04:53,882
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what birth is.

47
00:04:54,975 --> 00:04:57,756
[SPEAKER_01]: Birth is not coming out of womb.

48
00:04:58,416 --> 00:05:00,897
[SPEAKER_01]: Birth is manifesting.

49
00:05:00,937 --> 00:05:03,697
[SPEAKER_01]: Manifestation of the five aggregates through your appropriation.

50
00:05:04,197 --> 00:05:09,579
[SPEAKER_01]: And that starts, when the Buddha said himself, that starts when an embryo is conceived.

51
00:05:10,119 --> 00:05:14,500
[SPEAKER_01]: It's already, one is already manifested into this human realm.

52
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:20,502
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what we take to be birth, coming out of womb, in a hospital, is just like one of the

53
00:05:23,842 --> 00:05:30,768
[SPEAKER_01]: But they wouldn't be coming out of womb if there was no embryo conceived in the first place.

54
00:05:31,769 --> 00:05:37,414
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the birth takes place when the five aggregates manifest, when the five aggregates are bound.

55
00:05:37,454 --> 00:05:44,641
[SPEAKER_01]: Sorry, when the one to be bound is present, and mother and father come together, and mother is in season.

56
00:05:46,079 --> 00:05:47,400
[SPEAKER_01]: And then embryo is conceived.

57
00:05:47,540 --> 00:05:49,061
[SPEAKER_01]: Embryo, that is the five aggregates.

58
00:05:49,441 --> 00:05:50,842
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what birth is.

59
00:05:50,862 --> 00:06:03,770
[SPEAKER_01]: And that embryo, when it's conceived, simultaneously with its conception, or rather, simultaneously with its manifestation, another thing that manifests simultaneously to that, is aging and death.

60
00:06:06,512 --> 00:06:10,895
[SPEAKER_01]: Because growing of the embryo, it's already aging.

61
00:06:10,915 --> 00:06:11,835
[SPEAKER_01]: It's already dying.

62
00:06:12,876 --> 00:06:14,237
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it's manifested.

63
00:06:15,486 --> 00:06:20,048
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's a simultaneous presence of manifestation, aging and death.

64
00:06:22,889 --> 00:06:25,171
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that is the important thing to understand.

65
00:06:31,093 --> 00:06:42,999
[SPEAKER_01]: With dependent origination, it's not the explanation of causality, because every dependent origination description starts with, with this, this is.

66
00:06:45,324 --> 00:06:47,065
[SPEAKER_01]: So, with, yeah, two aspects.

67
00:06:47,165 --> 00:06:49,845
[SPEAKER_01]: One that determines the other, but both are present.

68
00:06:50,806 --> 00:06:51,866
[SPEAKER_01]: Simultaneously present.

69
00:06:52,166 --> 00:06:52,726
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what it means.

70
00:06:52,826 --> 00:06:54,627
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't involve time.

71
00:06:54,867 --> 00:06:56,107
[SPEAKER_01]: It's akālika.

72
00:06:56,628 --> 00:06:57,288
[SPEAKER_01]: It's timeless.

73
00:06:57,388 --> 00:06:58,388
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't involve time.

74
00:07:00,809 --> 00:07:07,451
[SPEAKER_01]: Things that don't involve time are the ones that are, like, in the relationship, are the ones that are simultaneously present to the same extent.

75
00:07:12,312 --> 00:07:14,173
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what proper attention shows you.

76
00:07:15,763 --> 00:07:17,004
[SPEAKER_01]: With this, this is.

77
00:07:18,345 --> 00:07:33,233
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's why, if somebody has a right view, all they need to do is practice proper attention, because all they need to do is just bring back to the mind that simultaneous principle of dependent origination.

78
00:07:35,515 --> 00:07:38,656
[SPEAKER_01]: And that will bring all the lust to fade.

79
00:07:42,599 --> 00:07:43,679
[SPEAKER_01]: All aversion to fade.

80
00:07:43,839 --> 00:07:44,800
[SPEAKER_01]: All ignorance to fade.

81
00:07:46,999 --> 00:07:52,422
[SPEAKER_00]: Because it says whatever he intends to, he intends rightly, and therefore... Yeah.

82
00:07:52,603 --> 00:07:58,226
[SPEAKER_01]: Whatever he intends to, he intends rightly, he intends properly, he intends according to its nature.

83
00:07:59,367 --> 00:08:01,168
[SPEAKER_01]: And that nature is, it is determined.

84
00:08:01,849 --> 00:08:02,909
[SPEAKER_01]: It is impermanent.

85
00:08:04,630 --> 00:08:10,314
[SPEAKER_01]: With this, this is.

86
00:08:10,414 --> 00:08:13,076
[SPEAKER_00]: I'll read the... Majjhima Kāyā.

87
00:08:14,486 --> 00:08:14,666
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

88
00:08:14,686 --> 00:08:14,907
[SPEAKER_00]: 2.

89
00:08:15,227 --> 00:08:15,768
[SPEAKER_00]: All the taints.

90
00:08:16,008 --> 00:08:19,852
[SPEAKER_00]: Because this goes into using proper attention.

91
00:08:20,933 --> 00:08:21,454
[SPEAKER_00]: Sure.

92
00:08:21,594 --> 00:08:25,017
[SPEAKER_00]: Attending to different things.

93
00:08:30,703 --> 00:08:33,887
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this is the Sābhāsana Sutta.

94
00:08:34,127 --> 00:08:34,748
[SPEAKER_00]: All the taints.

95
00:08:36,831 --> 00:08:40,475
[SPEAKER_00]: bhikkhus, I shall teach you a discourse on the restraint of all the taints.

96
00:08:41,055 --> 00:08:43,618
[SPEAKER_00]: Listen and tend closely to what I shall say.

97
00:08:44,499 --> 00:08:46,201
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, Venerable Sir, the bhikkhus replied.

98
00:08:46,521 --> 00:08:47,582
[SPEAKER_00]: The Vesubhan said this.

99
00:08:48,603 --> 00:08:55,130
[SPEAKER_00]: Bhikkhus, I say that the destruction of the taints is for one who knows and sees, not for one who does not know and see.

100
00:08:55,951 --> 00:08:58,193
[SPEAKER_00]: Means it's for... at least for the... for the...

101
00:08:59,339 --> 00:09:00,440
[SPEAKER_00]: Who knows and sees what?

102
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:03,582
[SPEAKER_00]: Proper attention and improper attention.

103
00:09:03,982 --> 00:09:04,403
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

104
00:09:04,583 --> 00:09:09,446
[SPEAKER_00]: When one attends properly, unarisen taints...

105
00:09:10,227 --> 00:09:17,592
[SPEAKER_00]: When one attends improperly, improperly, improperly, unarisen taints arise and arisen taints increase.

106
00:09:18,392 --> 00:09:24,937
[SPEAKER_00]: When one attends properly, unarisen taints do not arise and arisen taints are abandoned.

107
00:09:26,697 --> 00:09:35,263
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, the taints are three essential desires being in ignorance.

108
00:09:39,606 --> 00:09:55,777
[SPEAKER_00]: Because there are taints that should be abandoned by seeing, there are taints that should be abandoned by restraining, by using, by enduring, by avoiding, by removing, and by developing.

109
00:09:58,610 --> 00:09:59,991
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it goes on to each of those.

110
00:10:01,151 --> 00:10:03,072
[SPEAKER_00]: Taints to be abandoned by seeing.

111
00:10:05,053 --> 00:10:07,534
[SPEAKER_00]: What taints should be abandoned by seeing?

112
00:10:08,394 --> 00:10:16,358
[SPEAKER_00]: Here Bhikkhu is an untaught ordinary person, who has no regard for noble ones and is unskilled and undisciplined in their dhamma.

113
00:10:17,302 --> 00:10:26,248
[SPEAKER_00]: Who has no regard for true men and is unskilled and undisciplined in their dhamma, does not understand what things are fit for attention and what things are unfit for attention.

114
00:10:27,068 --> 00:10:34,973
[SPEAKER_00]: Since that is so, he attends to those things unfit for attention, and he does not attend to those things fit for attention.

115
00:10:34,993 --> 00:10:37,315
[SPEAKER_00]: What are the things unfit for attention that he attends to?

116
00:10:37,755 --> 00:10:43,079
[SPEAKER_00]: They are things such that, when he attends to them, the unarisen taint of sensual desire arises,

117
00:10:44,187 --> 00:10:49,471
[SPEAKER_00]: The taint of being arises, the taint of ignorance arises.

118
00:10:50,712 --> 00:10:53,114
[SPEAKER_00]: These are the things, unfit for attention, that he attends to.

119
00:10:56,597 --> 00:11:02,882
[SPEAKER_00]: And, eh, it's the opposite when he knows what he's doing, you know.

120
00:11:02,942 --> 00:11:12,750
[SPEAKER_00]: But the the untaught ordinary person also attends in this improper way.

121
00:11:13,870 --> 00:11:15,750
[SPEAKER_00]: He thinks to himself, was I in the past?

122
00:11:16,410 --> 00:11:17,411
[SPEAKER_00]: Was I not in the past?

123
00:11:18,291 --> 00:11:19,651
[SPEAKER_00]: Was I in the past?

124
00:11:19,891 --> 00:11:20,911
[SPEAKER_00]: How was I in the past?

125
00:11:20,931 --> 00:11:25,552
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the crucial difference.

126
00:11:26,512 --> 00:11:36,354
[SPEAKER_01]: Improper attention is the attention that carries the sense of self, carries the notion of I am.

127
00:11:39,234 --> 00:11:41,655
[SPEAKER_01]: Proper attention is the attention that

128
00:11:43,502 --> 00:11:46,024
[SPEAKER_01]: It leaves no room for the sense of self.

129
00:11:47,485 --> 00:11:57,753
[SPEAKER_01]: If you properly attend, if you say, with this, this is, there is no room for the owner of either this or this, or this or that, or in between the two.

130
00:11:58,233 --> 00:11:59,314
[SPEAKER_01]: There is just no room for it.

131
00:12:00,034 --> 00:12:02,936
[SPEAKER_01]: It's with the rising of this, this also rises.

132
00:12:03,497 --> 00:12:07,540
[SPEAKER_01]: Or rather with this, when this is present, this is present too.

133
00:12:08,801 --> 00:12:10,322
[SPEAKER_01]: So, basically, eh...

134
00:12:11,869 --> 00:12:25,418
[SPEAKER_01]: Fundamentally, you can take your experience as a whole and you can see that it's utterly, completely determined by the presence of light.

135
00:12:25,518 --> 00:12:26,158
[SPEAKER_01]: You can say that.

136
00:12:26,859 --> 00:12:28,080
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, you are alive.

137
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:31,742
[SPEAKER_01]: Thus, whatever you experience is because you're still alive.

138
00:12:33,123 --> 00:12:36,105
[SPEAKER_01]: Whatever you're experiencing, no matter what

139
00:12:38,217 --> 00:12:44,541
[SPEAKER_01]: No matter how it differs particularly, the nature of experience is there, because life is still present.

140
00:12:45,681 --> 00:12:50,164
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can... you can then just reflect further and say, okay, well, are you in control of that life?

141
00:12:51,064 --> 00:12:52,865
[SPEAKER_01]: Are you in control of the beating heart?

142
00:12:54,006 --> 00:12:55,827
[SPEAKER_01]: Are you in control of functional brain?

143
00:12:56,287 --> 00:12:59,149
[SPEAKER_01]: Are you in control of preventing accidents from happening?

144
00:12:59,289 --> 00:12:59,629
[SPEAKER_01]: You're not.

145
00:13:00,050 --> 00:13:02,211
[SPEAKER_01]: Thus, this life that is present,

146
00:13:04,792 --> 00:13:08,956
[SPEAKER_01]: It rests upon the foundations that are utterly inconceivable, inaccessible to you.

147
00:13:10,417 --> 00:13:13,920
[SPEAKER_01]: And when you fully understand that, then you cannot possibly regard it as yours.

148
00:13:15,021 --> 00:13:16,903
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's what proper attention penetrates.

149
00:13:17,524 --> 00:13:23,309
[SPEAKER_01]: It discerns that there are foundations that undermine you, that you cannot access.

150
00:13:24,250 --> 00:13:27,693
[SPEAKER_01]: So, basically, it restores the right order of things.

151
00:13:29,160 --> 00:13:31,062
[SPEAKER_01]: Whereby, with this, this is.

152
00:13:31,362 --> 00:13:32,283
[SPEAKER_01]: That is the right order.

153
00:13:32,803 --> 00:13:35,585
[SPEAKER_01]: For putrūjana, it's with me, my experience is.

154
00:13:37,587 --> 00:13:39,228
[SPEAKER_01]: I am, thus things are for me.

155
00:13:39,849 --> 00:13:40,570
[SPEAKER_01]: Things are mine.

156
00:13:41,010 --> 00:13:42,151
[SPEAKER_01]: It's actually the other way around.

157
00:13:44,693 --> 00:13:56,203
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's exactly why in that sutra it says, like, somebody who is a putrūjana, uninstructed worldling, who doesn't know how to attend to things properly,

